From: benjamin <benjamin.hien@web.de>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Experiment switch: crossing hook on the kernel's grid
 (PHOTONIC_ROUTER_CROSSING_HOOK_KERNEL_GRID=1)

The live crossing hook builds its own dense grid from the obstacle map with
no port-open cells, dynamic expansion radius 0 and no clearance-exempt
cells, while the kernel's search grid gets all three (speed pass A8 found
the difference: a halo dedupe that read the kernel grid moved three gate
cells). With the switch on, CrossingHookContext::build takes the kernel's
inputs (anchor open cells, dynamic radius, exempt cells) for its grid too.

Off (default): nine-cell gate identical to the previous commit in every
metric. On: crossings and errors unchanged on the nine cells, three lengths
shorter (Benes 8x8 baseline 31418.224 -> 31409.94 um, ADEPT 8x8 baseline
25171.624 -> 24921.086, contribution 1 25090.058 -> 24969.384); the 27-cell
table decides whether this becomes the default (then the switch goes).
Read once per process; experiment-only, not part of the config overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0152GWPQy8AyTgwk6GNvQ3qH
